<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dictyostelium discoideum Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.304 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Dictyostelium discoideum)",
        "Dictyostelium discoideum Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.304 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Dictyostelium discoideum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dictyostelium discoideum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dictyostelium discoideum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Taniguchi phase singularities or mass-conserving Brauns–Frey kinetics were integrated.",
        "does_not_claim: That a paper measured λ = 2.304 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Lean file was checked by the Lean kernel; lean was not installed.",
        "does_not_claim: That the sorocarp silhouette is the cortical Turing field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Schnakenberg PDE, discrete-Laplacian dispersion, δ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and border-contrast segmentation of the vendored sorocarp.",
        "reported_in_source: Höfer 1995 and Sawai 2005: extracellular cAMP organizes millimetre-scale aggregation.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: trimolecular kinetics used as the carrier of k_c.",
        "reported_in_source: Taniguchi 2013 and Bretschneider 2009: Dictyostelium cortical actin/PIP3 waves are a few-micrometre excitable pattern.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.304 µm (2.304e-06 m, log10=-5.638, tier 3_subcellular_um, detail) is the slot coordinate. Age is 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1.",
        "transfer_boundary: A 200 nm predecessor regime admits N=0. A 1 mm aggregation successor is a longer wavelength of the same extant species." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Dictyostelium discoideum; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: trimolecular kinetics used as the carrier of k_c. | Taniguchi 2013 and Bretschneider 2009: Dictyostelium cortical actin/PIP3 waves are a few-micrometre excitable pattern. | Höfer 1995 and Sawai 2005: extracellular cAMP organizes millimetre-scale aggregation.; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Schnakenberg PDE, discrete-Laplacian dispersion, δ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and border-contrast segmentation of the vendored sorocarp.; transfer_boundary: 2.304 µm (2.304e-06 m, log10=-5.638, tier 3_subcellular_um, detail) is the slot coordinate. Age is 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1. | A 200 nm predecessor regime admits N=0. A 1 mm aggregation successor is a longer wavelength of the same extant species.; does_not_claim: That a paper measured λ = 2.304 µm. | That the sorocarp silhouette is the cortical Turing field. | That Taniguchi phase singularities or mass-conserving Brauns–Frey kinetics were integrated. | That the Lean file was checked by the Lean kernel; lean was not installed.]; phenomenon_size: 205 µm (0.0002048 m, log10=-3.689 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 205 µm to 205 µm): 205 µm:limit-cycle-turing" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2008.12.3942>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03228>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1218025110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1995.0037>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
